docs {
  ## Settlement receipt access

  SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT is always private. Unbound files are uploader-only. Bound PENDING/CANCELED files are visible only to the active sender/recipient; SUCCESS/REJECT files are visible to all active group members. Former/inactive members have no access. This applies to metadata, streams, batch URLs, ZIP and group lists. No owner/admin override. Direct deletion of any bound payment receipt returns 409 SETTLEMENT_RECEIPT_LOCKED; delete its PENDING payment first. No receipt edits are supported.

  Upload/confirm omit settlement_id and expense_id; link uploaded IDs through Create Settlement. SETTLING groups allow settlement receipt uploads; CLOSED does not. Presigned confirmation validates actual MIME and size, then creates a separate server-controlled object. Never re-confirm an already registered receipt key. See the Settlements folder for the complete workflow and errors.

  # Get Attachment Details
  
  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/attachments/:id`
  **Auth:** Optional (`OptionalAuth` middleware). Public attachments require no auth; private attachments require Bearer token of uploader or group member.
  
  ## Description
  
  Retrieves detailed metadata for a specific attachment by its primary key ID, including dimensions, file hash, and an active access URL.
  
  EXPENSE_RECEIPT is never publicly readable through these APIs. An unbound receipt is accessible only to its uploader. A linked receipt requires an ACTIVE account and ACTIVE membership with left_at=null in the expense group, including when the uploader is requesting it; former members lose access. Inactive groups still allow receipt reads. Site ADMIN alone grants no bypass. Signed URLs already issued remain usable until expiry.

  ## Request
  
  ### Path Parameters
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `id` | `int64` | Yes | Attachment primary key ID |
  
  ### Query Parameters
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `expiry` | `string` | No | Presigned URL duration (e.g. `15m`, `1h`, `24h`; defaults to `1h`) |
  
  ### Headers
  
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Optional | Bearer access token (required for private files) |

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 1,
      "uploader_user_id": 1,
      "group_id": 1,
      "type": "GALLERY_IMAGE",
      "original_filename": "photo.jpg",
      "file_size_bytes": 1048576,
      "mime_type": "image/jpeg",
      "sha256_hash": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855",
      "is_public": false,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1080,
      "access_url": "https://storage.example.com/uploads/photo.jpg?X-Amz-Signature=...",
      "created_at": "2026-11-02T19:00:00Z"
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Invalid attachment ID format
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Authentication required to view private attachment
  * `403 Forbidden` — Access denied to private attachment
  * `404 Not Found` — Attachment not found
}
